WEBVTT

00:10.080 --> 00:11.070
<i>I've seen it now.</i>

00:11.730 --> 00:15.570
<i>With my superior eyesight...
I've seen what the Medusa truly is.</i>

00:16.500 --> 00:19.540
<i>Senku, you were right.</i>

00:19.900 --> 00:23.140
<i>It isn't any kind of curse or 
demonic device devoid of rules.</i>

00:24.380 --> 00:26.320
<i>The petrification weapon, the Medusa...</i>

00:28.420 --> 00:29.250
<i>is science.</i>

00:35.030 --> 00:36.740
<i>It's up to you now, Amaryllis.</i>

00:36.740 --> 00:38.930
<i>Tell Senku and the others.</i>

00:39.580 --> 00:42.590
<i>Tell them all the secrets that 
the infiltration team has found.</i>

00:44.970 --> 00:47.640
So long as we're fighting 
with science, we're ahead.

00:49.130 --> 00:53.060
All that's left now is to trust 
science and the others, and wait.

00:54.570 --> 00:55.370
Yeah.

00:56.540 --> 00:58.810
Everything's gonna be fine.

02:37.280 --> 02:42.010
<b>Deal Game, Test of Wit</b>

02:52.100 --> 02:54.320
m 0 0 l 160 0 l 160 80 l 0 80

02:52.100 --> 02:54.320
Yuzuriha
is revived!!

02:58.520 --> 03:01.070
Yuzuriha!

03:00.170 --> 03:01.070
Taiju-kun!

03:03.120 --> 03:04.550
No! Just a handshake!

03:04.550 --> 03:07.390
Gotta be respectful, even with close friends!

03:09.130 --> 03:12.120
What are you, a hover-handing 
middle school kid?

03:15.920 --> 03:18.050
I wonder if this is part of Chrome.

03:22.180 --> 03:24.140
m 0 0 l 160 0 l 160 80 l 0 80

03:22.180 --> 03:24.140
Chrome is
 revived!!

03:24.500 --> 03:26.520
She's crazy good at this.

03:26.520 --> 03:31.770
Her memory and crafts club experience makes 
her even faster with the jigsaw puzzle.

03:32.820 --> 03:36.600
Oh, man! That was my first time 
experiencing petrification!

03:36.600 --> 03:38.520
So that's what it's like!

03:38.520 --> 03:41.100
Same reaction as Kaseki-chan.

03:42.190 --> 03:44.610
Birds of a feather!

03:44.610 --> 03:47.660
Chrome and I are the builder duo.

03:48.040 --> 03:49.370
So anyway...

03:49.370 --> 03:50.950
Now that you're awake,

03:50.950 --> 03:54.090
I'm gonna need you to get right 
back to building stuff with me.

03:54.090 --> 03:55.290
Oh, shit!

03:55.510 --> 03:58.880
We're all set for the drone-building team now.

03:58.880 --> 04:02.580
This marks the beginning of 
our three-dimensional war.

04:03.230 --> 04:04.150
Which means...

04:05.200 --> 04:07.490
We need our 3D specialist!

04:07.490 --> 04:08.430
Am I right?

04:14.140 --> 04:16.100
m 0 0 l 160 0 l 160 80 l 0 80

04:14.140 --> 04:16.100
Ukyo is
 revived!!

04:20.360 --> 04:21.070
I see.

04:21.470 --> 04:24.410
What we really want now is information, then.

04:24.410 --> 04:25.290
On the enemy.

04:26.420 --> 04:30.100
Of course you would say that, 
former sonar operator.

04:31.450 --> 04:34.270
We've got you covered. 
Kohaku and her team's in the enem—

04:34.270 --> 04:34.830
Hold it.

04:38.330 --> 04:39.280
Someone's coming.

04:41.080 --> 04:42.460
They're swimming through the water.

04:50.820 --> 04:52.420
Amaryllis-chan!

04:52.420 --> 04:53.440
Everyone...

04:53.760 --> 04:54.940
It's Kohaku-chan and...

04:55.560 --> 04:58.010
Kohaku-chan and Ginro!

05:36.970 --> 05:41.540
So Soyuz was part of the Master's family?

05:45.000 --> 05:48.160
Though it's only by Ginro's 
estimation that you look alike.

05:49.740 --> 05:54.080
Yeah, there's no point in 
speculating about that now.

05:54.080 --> 05:59.710
What I want to know is the enemy's 
capabilities and internal affairs.

06:01.630 --> 06:06.320
We'll use our intellect to make the most 
of the little bits of information we have.

06:06.680 --> 06:07.820
Leave that to me!

06:07.820 --> 06:09.820
I got this!

06:09.820 --> 06:12.470
Good. Let's start by organizing our information.

06:12.470 --> 06:16.430
Man, the Kingdom of Science 
is finally back together.

06:16.970 --> 06:18.440
This is awesome!

06:18.440 --> 06:22.310
Now that I look at it, it's that 
team Kohaku was talking about...

06:22.610 --> 06:25.090
The five cleverest people in the kingdom.

06:26.060 --> 06:28.570
It's a meeting of the 
Kingdom of Science brass!

06:30.200 --> 06:32.390
Good job, Amaryllis.

06:32.390 --> 06:35.740
You and the spy team put in some nice work.

06:35.740 --> 06:38.420
You've leaked a top secret to us.

06:39.250 --> 06:45.250
The enemy's only got one 
petrification weapon.

06:47.510 --> 06:50.560
I see. That's critical information.

06:50.560 --> 06:52.370
Indeed.

06:52.370 --> 06:55.260
Put yourself in Ibara-chan's shoes.

06:55.260 --> 06:58.460
Well, it's not for certain, 
but we do need a working hypothesis.

06:58.460 --> 07:04.500
Hang on, what's this 
"oh, yeah, I totally get it" vibe?

07:04.500 --> 07:05.900
I don't get it!

07:06.320 --> 07:09.400
How can you know from 
what I just told you?

07:09.680 --> 07:12.170
Senku says so, so it must be true.

07:12.170 --> 07:14.030
That's an optimistic resignation.

07:14.670 --> 07:16.950
No, you lot need to hear this, too.

07:18.590 --> 07:22.630
This is a painstaking puzzle made up 
of bits of unrelated information.

07:22.940 --> 07:26.020
You saw how fast Soyuz and Yuzuriha were

07:26.020 --> 07:28.430
at putting it together 
when they worked together.

07:28.430 --> 07:30.400
We may, for example,

07:31.440 --> 07:35.040
need Chrome's power of intuition.

07:35.040 --> 07:38.040
You stuck-up prick.

07:38.040 --> 07:40.000
All right! I'll do it.

07:43.520 --> 07:46.940
First, the Master doesn't 
have a petrification weapon.

07:46.940 --> 07:49.610
Well, yeah, he's petrified.

07:49.610 --> 07:52.610
Doesn't Ibara have it, though? 
He runs the show.

07:52.610 --> 07:53.480
Yeah.

07:53.480 --> 07:55.530
Ibara is very cautious.

07:55.530 --> 07:57.030
He must have one.

07:57.030 --> 07:58.990
That's where the trick is.

07:59.480 --> 08:03.070
Ibara-chan's the type who has insurance 
policy upon insurance policy.

08:03.070 --> 08:07.710
If there's another petrification 
weapon, he'd be the one to have it.

08:07.950 --> 08:11.230
He was in a hurry to petrify the intruders.

08:11.230 --> 08:15.450
Why didn't he have his own ready to go?

08:16.030 --> 08:17.260
You're right.

08:18.030 --> 08:20.770
I'm amazed you picked that 
up from such a little hint.

08:21.720 --> 08:24.190
In other words, there's only 
one petrification weapon.

08:25.350 --> 08:28.300
That was complicated, but I 
understand the conclusion!

08:28.300 --> 08:31.530
The thrower's at risk of being petrified, too.

08:31.530 --> 08:35.740
Ibara-sama, being as cautious as 
he is, lets Kirisame do it instead.

08:35.970 --> 08:38.830
Wh-What a nasty old man!

08:39.310 --> 08:43.190
There's one important 
thing I want to confirm.

08:43.190 --> 08:44.240
Amaryllis.

08:45.160 --> 08:46.540
About the third dimension.

08:47.110 --> 08:53.040
You said the petrification weapon Kirisame 
threw created a blast from above, right?

08:53.040 --> 08:54.420
That's right.

08:55.720 --> 08:57.130
I see...

08:57.130 --> 09:03.310
If Kirisame-chan had to avoid 
the Master when she threw it...

09:03.540 --> 09:07.890
That's a stupidly important 
piece of information, too.

09:08.540 --> 09:12.900
Kirisame doesn't know the Master is a statue.

09:14.470 --> 09:16.740
You're right, but...

09:16.740 --> 09:18.780
How did you find out?

09:18.780 --> 09:19.660
I'm impressed.

09:19.660 --> 09:20.630
<i>Moz!</i>

09:20.630 --> 09:22.880
<i>I didn't notice him even with my hearing!</i>

09:27.850 --> 09:28.750
Taiju-kun!

09:33.040 --> 09:36.220
You've got some endurance.

09:37.000 --> 09:41.660
But that's only going to buy you some time.

09:42.120 --> 09:45.480
What are you going to do now?

09:46.010 --> 09:48.130
<i>Yeah, buying some time.</i>

09:48.130 --> 09:50.920
<i>That's what we need the most.</i>

09:50.920 --> 09:54.280
<i>Get your head in full gear with 
the few seconds Taiju gave you!</i>

09:54.860 --> 09:57.610
<i>I know because I'm hungry for people's power.</i>

09:58.400 --> 10:02.100
<i>Going all-in against him won't change a thing.</i>

10:02.410 --> 10:04.360
<i>This is bad.</i>

10:04.360 --> 10:05.480
<i>We're pretty screwed.</i>

10:05.480 --> 10:07.250
<i>Is there really a way out of this?</i>

10:07.640 --> 10:10.700
<i>I need to get at least one of us out alive.</i>

10:11.840 --> 10:13.140
I'm sorry...

10:13.140 --> 10:16.130
I must have been followed.

10:19.590 --> 10:22.930
<i>I've always been a scavenger, 
ever since I was a kid.</i>

10:22.930 --> 10:24.910
<i>I know better than anyone</i>

10:24.910 --> 10:29.730
<i>how much of a pain in the ass it 
is to look for stuff in the dark.</i>

10:30.260 --> 10:34.540
<i>He followed Amaryllis after she put 
herself through so much to escape...</i>

10:34.540 --> 10:36.440
<i>And he didn't kill her?</i>

10:37.420 --> 10:39.150
That bastard Moz...

10:39.440 --> 10:43.200
He must have known Amaryllis's 
group were intruders.

10:43.770 --> 10:47.290
Wait, why are you stating the 
obvious now, Chrome-chan?

10:47.290 --> 10:48.850
He obviously knew.

10:48.850 --> 10:53.530
Kohaku-chan was already outed, 
so everyone with her had to be...

10:54.000 --> 10:56.190
<i>That's it! That means...</i>

10:56.190 --> 10:59.660
<i>He knew Ginro was an intruder, too!</i>

10:59.660 --> 11:04.390
<i>That's some huge information 
to keep from Ibara.</i>

11:05.350 --> 11:13.190
<i>Ibara and an intruder were facing off 
one-on-one, and Moz just sat there watching.</i>

11:13.840 --> 11:17.280
<i>Which means Moz doesn't mind if Ibara dies.</i>

11:17.280 --> 11:20.010
<i>Or he even plans to kill him.</i>

11:22.810 --> 11:28.290
All the puzzle pieces are coming 
together in this knowledge battle.

11:28.290 --> 11:31.160
I see the whole state of 
the Petrification Kingdom.

11:31.500 --> 11:34.450
We have a shot at tearing them down, then.

11:34.450 --> 11:35.840
Who's...

11:42.140 --> 11:44.630
Of course.

11:47.840 --> 11:50.520
Heya...

11:50.910 --> 11:52.510
Just give us...

11:52.510 --> 11:55.330
Just give us a second, Moz-chan.

11:56.170 --> 11:58.570
I've got a good offer for you.

11:59.460 --> 12:05.010
How about you and we, 
the Kingdom of Science, join forces?

12:05.010 --> 12:07.420
Wouldn't that be exhilarating?

12:28.930 --> 12:32.110
What do you think of our bird of witchcraft?

12:32.110 --> 12:35.870
We can fly this thing however we want.

12:35.870 --> 12:40.580
We can grab Kirisame-chan's petrification 
weapon in the air, no problem!

12:41.520 --> 12:43.320
"However we want" is a 
bit of an overstatement.

12:43.930 --> 12:47.590
It's not even stable yet. 
It's just an electric bamboo copter.

12:47.590 --> 12:49.830
Don't worry about it, Senku-chan.

12:50.490 --> 12:53.800
<i>You pretend your weak card is 
actually your ace of spades.</i>

12:53.800 --> 12:57.750
<i>That's the first move in any 
negotiation, in any deal making.</i>

12:58.150 --> 13:02.090
<i>If we fought Moz, we'd all die.</i>

13:03.530 --> 13:05.020
<i>Think about it another way!</i>

13:05.020 --> 13:08.720
<i>This is an opportunity to negotiate with 
the strongest man and get him on our side!</i>

13:10.150 --> 13:13.730
<i>Everything's riding on your flimsy word.</i>

13:13.980 --> 13:16.900
<i>Shit! Please, Gen!</i>

13:17.210 --> 13:20.170
If you and I, sorcerers, team up,

13:20.170 --> 13:25.370
we could end up taking over this island 
and the inner palace for ourselves!

13:21.660 --> 13:24.500
<i>When did Gen get over there?!</i>

13:25.920 --> 13:27.910
Don't you think?

13:28.370 --> 13:33.160
<b>Mentalist Gen's</b>

13:28.370 --> 13:33.160
<b>Manipulation Techniques</b>

13:29.200 --> 13:33.160
Mentalist Gen's manipulation techniques!

13:33.470 --> 13:36.220
This one's pretty famous.

13:36.220 --> 13:41.210
People feel more solidarity with you if 
you're next to them, not opposite them.

13:41.210 --> 13:44.660
That's why they tell you to take 
a counter seat instead of a table.

13:46.780 --> 13:49.890
<i>So the first move of having 
him look up at the drone</i>

13:49.890 --> 13:54.320
<i>segues naturally into his next 
move of standing next to him.</i>

13:54.320 --> 13:56.640
<i>Not bad, mentalist.</i>

13:57.210 --> 14:01.680
I mean, you're so strong, Moz-chan.

14:02.010 --> 14:06.650
If Ibara-chan and all those 
other soldiers are a hundred,

14:06.650 --> 14:11.160
you're probably a hundred fifty.

14:11.160 --> 14:13.980
<i>No, he's way more than that!</i>

14:16.350 --> 14:19.000
Maybe a little more than that.

14:20.650 --> 14:30.220
<b>Mentalist Gen's</b>

14:20.650 --> 14:30.220
<b>Manipulation Techniques</b>

14:21.380 --> 14:24.890
Mentalist Gen's manipulation techniques!

14:24.890 --> 14:26.240
Number two!

14:26.710 --> 14:30.220
Try saying something that's 
a little bit off-the-mark.

14:30.870 --> 14:34.400
The urge to correct you will 
be so strong that they might

14:34.400 --> 14:38.350
sign on to something they never intended to.

14:38.350 --> 14:42.420
<i>In reality, they're probably worlds apart.</i>

14:42.420 --> 14:43.690
<i>I want him!</i>

14:43.690 --> 14:44.520
Wow!

14:44.520 --> 14:50.780
If you're really that strong, you could 
take Ibara-chan out easy, right?

14:52.870 --> 14:57.540
<i>Although I kinda get the sense 
that he's seeing right through me.</i>

14:59.250 --> 15:04.210
Kill all of you, or kill Ibara...

15:06.390 --> 15:07.960
What to do?

15:10.560 --> 15:16.310
Well, if I'm going to kill all of you, 
there's no harm in telling you.

15:18.210 --> 15:24.940
I'm sure you've figured out by now that 
the one who petrified the Master...

15:25.860 --> 15:27.480
was Ibara.

15:28.090 --> 15:30.050
He's already done plenty of work.

15:30.050 --> 15:31.690
Good job, I suppose.

15:31.690 --> 15:34.390
It's about time that old fogy croaks, right?

15:34.820 --> 15:39.910
The girls would probably appreciate it 
if I made it my own inner palace, too.

15:41.540 --> 15:44.840
Why not go ahead and kill him, then?

15:45.290 --> 15:48.920
I would have done it long ago if 
not for the petrification beam.

15:49.220 --> 15:54.010
Kirisame-chan, who's handling the 
petrification weapon, is pretty strong.

15:54.420 --> 16:00.890
I'd win in a normal fight, but one shot from 
her unavoidable beam, and I'm done for.

16:01.670 --> 16:05.930
In other words, if you attack Minister Ibara,

16:05.930 --> 16:09.420
Kirisame, who doesn't know what's going on, 
would use her petrification beam on you.

16:09.830 --> 16:16.160
But if you exposed him, 
you'd lose access to the inner palace.

16:16.430 --> 16:19.370
You've got yourselves 
in a three-way deadlock.

16:20.910 --> 16:23.590
Ibara's got a good thing going for himself.

16:23.590 --> 16:25.610
He's not your regular old fart.

16:25.610 --> 16:29.380
I-I'm starting to have a hard time keeping up.

16:30.290 --> 16:33.670
To put it simply enough for 
a meathead to understand...

16:34.250 --> 16:37.720
Moz, you want the petrification beam gone.

16:38.370 --> 16:41.100
We want the petrification beam ourselves.

16:41.520 --> 16:46.550
Our interests are ten 
billion percent aligned.

16:48.360 --> 16:49.440
Bingo!

16:49.440 --> 16:51.930
It's the petrification weapon we want!

16:51.930 --> 16:54.700
A negotiation's gotta be 
on even footing, right?

16:54.700 --> 16:58.950
Why don't you take over the island and 
have the inner palace for yourself?

16:58.950 --> 17:03.440
We'll help with our sorcery, 
but only on one condition.

17:03.850 --> 17:07.910
You have to give us the petrification 
weapon. No exceptions.

17:07.910 --> 17:11.850
That's one thing that has 
to be absolute, Moz-chan!

17:11.850 --> 17:13.030
<i>The way he says it...</i>

17:13.030 --> 17:14.550
<i>He's so skeevy.</i>

17:14.550 --> 17:17.470
<i>I have a feeling this is going 
to make him more stubborn.</i>

17:18.550 --> 17:19.990
Even footing?

17:22.380 --> 17:25.130
I don't need to uphold any conditions, do I?

17:25.130 --> 17:28.350
I've got the upper hand in combat.

17:29.080 --> 17:32.800
You'll use your sorcery for my sake.

17:32.800 --> 17:35.360
And you'll give me the petrification weapon.

17:38.260 --> 17:39.800
That's awful, though!

17:39.800 --> 17:43.450
Hang on a minute, Moz-chan! Even footing!

17:41.910 --> 17:43.450
<i>I knew it!</i>

17:45.590 --> 17:48.670
I'll keep your hideout a secret.

17:48.670 --> 17:53.090
Your only choice is to do as I say.

18:00.850 --> 18:06.270
<b>Mentalist Gen's</b>

18:00.850 --> 18:06.270
<b>Manipulation
Techniques</b>

18:01.940 --> 18:05.120
Mentalist Gen's manipulation techniques!

18:05.120 --> 18:06.280
Number three!

18:06.890 --> 18:09.610
It's called psychological reactance.

18:09.610 --> 18:12.270
When you feel like you're 
being forced to do things,

18:12.270 --> 18:17.820
your need to maintain control 
causes you to reject things.

18:18.060 --> 18:19.150
I see!

18:19.150 --> 18:20.820
Gen's doing this on purpose!

18:21.520 --> 18:22.950
Think about it.

18:22.950 --> 18:24.520
The conversation's shifted.

18:24.520 --> 18:26.580
You're right.

18:27.290 --> 18:32.710
The conversation was originally whether 
he was going to kill us all or not.

18:33.370 --> 18:38.790
Psychological reactance has him refusing 
to do as this sleazy man wants.

18:38.790 --> 18:42.720
We're suddenly talking 
about working together.

18:44.020 --> 18:48.140
The way to win a deal isn't to make 
the other person feel defeated.

18:48.140 --> 18:53.780
It's to show servitude, setting out a 
false red carpet for them and stuff.

18:53.780 --> 18:55.470
That's what really matters.

19:04.620 --> 19:09.310
This is the earring Kohaku-chan 
was wearing, is it not?

19:10.330 --> 19:14.010
Kingdom of Sorcery headquarters here.

19:25.800 --> 19:27.200
He's gone, right?

19:27.730 --> 19:28.940
He's gone.

19:36.820 --> 19:39.130
Good going, mentalist!

19:41.290 --> 19:43.250
Thank you, thank you.

19:43.250 --> 19:47.340
But that means we've got the ultimate power!

19:47.340 --> 19:48.650
Am I right?

19:49.550 --> 19:54.650
Although he's probably ten billion percent 
set on killing all of us once we're done.

19:54.650 --> 19:58.250
We'll cross that bridge when we come to it.

19:59.540 --> 20:05.020
But can I just take a break for now?

20:05.180 --> 20:08.470
m 0 0 l 136 0 l 136 80 l 0 80

20:05.180 --> 20:08.470
Moz joined the
party (for now)!!

20:44.240 --> 20:46.590
You hearing me, Moz-sensei?

20:47.390 --> 20:49.680
Follow my directions.

20:50.100 --> 20:52.320
<i>You'll find treasure at the destination.</i>

20:55.830 --> 20:59.710
It's a super valuable gift we 
made for you using sorcery.

21:02.890 --> 21:07.450
We, Kingdom of Science members, 
are totally outnumbered.

21:07.450 --> 21:12.880
If they came at us with brute force, 
we'd be screwed instantly.

21:13.830 --> 21:19.700
So we need your strength to make 
them believe we're tough as hell.

21:20.150 --> 21:24.300
We need to force them to bring 
out the petrification weapon.

21:26.400 --> 21:27.780
In other words...

21:31.130 --> 21:34.180
A night raid, pretending to be an intruder.

21:50.170 --> 21:51.950
Don't kill him!

21:51.950 --> 21:54.660
Yeah! That's it! Get' em!

21:51.950 --> 21:54.670
Let him tell them how strong the enemy is!

21:54.670 --> 21:57.920
He always gets way too excited 
when it comes to his plots.

22:02.230 --> 22:04.230
I'm already on it.

22:05.310 --> 22:09.430
Oh, right. You can't hear me.

22:11.740 --> 22:13.900
Sorcery can be pretty inconvenient.

23:49.740 --> 23:52.410
<b>Battle in Three Dimensions</b>

23:51.950 --> 23:54.910
<b>Next Episode</b>

23:51.970 --> 23:54.910
<b>Battle in Three Dimensions</b>

23:54.910 --> 23:59.920
<b>This is a work of fiction, but the plants, 
animals, and production methods described are based on reality.
Foraging and making things on your own accord is extremely dangerous
and, in some cases, illegal. Please do not imitate without expertise.</b>
